Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
CODE DOCUMENTATION

File: Theory/Moments-calculations-FFL-OpenLoop.nb
Paper: An information-theoretic perspective on feed-forward loop abundances \
in transcriptional networks
Authors: Mintu Nandi, Sudip Chattopadhyay, and Suman K Banik
Contact: mintunandi@ubi.s.u-tokyo.ac.jp; sudip@chem.iiests.ac.in; \
skbanik@jcbose.ac.in

Purpose
Constructs the FFL and open-loop Jacobian, covariance, and diffusion \
matrices, solves the steady-state Lyapunov equations, and prints the variance \
and covariance relations used in the Supplementary Material.

How to run
Open the notebook in Wolfram Mathematica and evaluate the calculation groups. \
The notebook calls Quit[] at the end of each main group, so the groups can be \
evaluated separately.

Inputs and outputs
No external input files are required. Symbolic expressions are embedded in \
the notebook and the derived moment relations are returned as evaluated cells \
and printed output.

Code-to-manuscript notation
J -> manuscript Jacobian J; S -> covariance matrix Sigma; No -> diffusion \
matrix D; vx, vy, vz -> sigma_X^2, sigma_Y^2, sigma_Z^2; vxy, vxz, vyz -> the \
corresponding covariances; xav, yav, zav -> <x>, <y>, <z>; betax, betay, \
betaz -> beta_X, beta_Y, beta_Z; fyxp, fzxp, fzyp -> f'_YX, f'_ZX, f'_ZY.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9962824664318275`*^9, 3.996282469312643*^9}},
 Background->GrayLevel[
  0.95],ExpressionUUID->"75cf7f12-27b7-5d42-bc11-06b46b9f0143"],

